    <!-- Onboarding / disclosure (Requirement.md section 8: prominent disclosure before access). -->
    <string name="disclosure_title">Your messages stay on this phone</string>
    <string name="disclosure_body">To work as your SMS app, %1$s needs to read, send and receive your SMS messages, and show notifications for them. If you allow contacts, it also reads contact names and photos to label conversations.\n\nEverything is processed on this device. There are no accounts, no servers, no ads and no analytics. Message content is never shared or sold. If you turn on Google Drive backup, an encrypted copy that only you can unlock is kept in your own Drive.\n\nThe next step asks you to make %1$s your default SMS app. You can say Not now and still open the app; it will ask again next time.</string>
